= The 60-Second Self-Test

Cover the answers, say each one aloud, then check. If any answer takes longer than ten seconds, revisit that section.

- *The two challenges of 1947?* → Shape one nation out of the mosaic AND establish democracy — at the same time.
- *About how many refugees entered India after Partition?* → Around 80 lakh — the century's largest migration.
- *Which three subjects did rulers cede by the Instrument of Accession?* → Defence, external affairs, communications.
- *Match the holdouts to their endings.* → Junagadh — plebiscite 1948; Hyderabad — police action Sept 1948; Kashmir — accession Oct 1947 then war.
- *Which two bodies REJECTED language as the basis of states?* → Dhar Commission (1948) and the JVP Committee (1948-49).
- *Who fasted for Andhra, for how long, and with what result?* → Potti Sriramulu — 58 days — died 15 Dec 1952; Andhra State came in Oct 1953.
- *What did the SRC and the 1956 Act deliver?* → Language accepted with safeguards; 14 states + 6 union territories.
- *What did Nehru promise in 1959, and what law kept it?* → English stays as long as non-Hindi states want — the Official Languages Act 1963.
- *What happened in Madras in January 1965?* → Anti-Hindi agitation; self-immolations; Hindi was never imposed.
- *Why did Delhi hesitate on linguistic states right after 1947?* → Partition had just split the country on identity lines — language-based division looked like the same danger.
- *Name the two dimensions of the Kashmir problem.* → External (the India-Pakistan territorial rivalry) and internal (how much autonomy the state should enjoy).

